LOCATION:Lowell E. Baier Hall - Lecture Room - 125
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
SUMMARY:Gouged: A Conversation with Lindsay Owens on Price Gouging
DESCRIPTION:Why do prices go up quickly but come down slowly\, if they co
 me down at all? When does a price increase stop being normal market behav
 ior and become exploitation? The Antitrust and Consumer Protection Law As
 sociation invites you to an interview with Lindsay Owens\, author of Goug
 ed\, to explore those questions.  The interview will be followed by an au
 dience Q&amp\;A. Whether you're interested in antitrust\, consumer protec
 tion\, regulatory policy\, or simply understanding why everything costs m
 ore\, this event is a chance to engage directly with one of the leading v
 oices on corporate pricing power.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Why do prices go up quickly but come do
 wn slowly\, if they come down at all? When does a price increase stop bei
 ng normal market behavior and become exploitation? The Antitrust and Cons
 umer Protection Law Association invites you to an interview with Lindsay 
 Owens\, author of Gouged\, to explore those questions.<br />  The intervi
 ew will be followed by an audience Q&amp\;A. Whether you're interested in
  antitrust\, consumer protection\, regulatory policy\, or simply understa
 nding why everything costs more\, this event is a chance to engage direct
 ly with one of the leading voices on corporate pricing power.</p>
UID:20261102T170000Z-2466348@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20261028T125155Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2466348-gouged-a-conversation-with
 -lindsay-owens-on-price
LAST-MODIFIED:20261028T214622Z
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2466348
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>Robert Martin<br />\nAntitrust &amp\; Consume
 r Protection Law Assc</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:Antitrust &amp\; Consumer Protection Law Association
END:VEVENT
