DTSTART:20261105T170000Z
DTEND:20261105T180000Z
LOCATION:Lowell E. Baier Hall - DeLaney Moot Court Room - 123
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
SUMMARY:Originalism in the Courtroom: How History Should Guide Modern Cri
 minal Law
DESCRIPTION:Join Marc Levin\, Chief Policy Counsel for the Council on Cri
 minal Justice and Senior Advisor for Right on Crime\, and the Federalist 
 Society for a discussion of originalism in the courtroom\, exploring how 
 history and constitutional interpretation inform modern criminal justice\
 , the rights of defendants\, and the limits of government power.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join Marc Levin\, Chief Policy Counsel 
 for the Council on Criminal Justice and Senior Advisor for Right on Crime
 \, and the Federalist Society for a discussion of originalism in the cour
 troom\, exploring how history and constitutional interpretation inform mo
 dern criminal justice\, the rights of defendants\, and the limits of gove
 rnment power.</p>
