BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Maurer School of Law
DTSTART:20261120T144500Z
DTEND:20261120T220000Z
LOCATION:LOWELL E. BAIER HALL/IU MAURER SCHOOL OF LAW
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
SUMMARY:IJGLS Symposium
DESCRIPTION:Climate change\, pollution\, and biodiversity loss are intens
 ifying worldwide\, and their heaviest burdens fall on the world's most vu
 lnerable populations and indigenous communities. An estimated 1.5 billion
  people lack basic access to redress for environmental harms through poli
 tical\, administrative\, or legal channels. Many of these communities als
 o lack skilled advocates\, and the lawyers and nonlawyers who do take up 
 their causes face growing harassment and physical attacks. The Indiana Jo
 urnal of Global Legal Studies has brought together scholars from across t
 he Americas to examine where marginalized communities\, their advocates\,
  and the governance systems that too often leave them behind intersect.  
 &#160\;Panel 1: Environmental Protection Across Borders: Who Shapes the R
 ules\, and Who Gets Heard?Panel 2: Effective Environmental Representation
 : Bridging the Gap Between Rights and ResultsPanel 3: Environmental Gover
 nance Frameworks: What Do Comprehensive Solutions Look Like?Panel 4: In P
 ractice: Applying Environmental Rights and Supporting Environmental Defen
 ders  Papers presented at the symposium will be published in Volume 34 Is
 sue 2 of the Journal.&#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Climate change\, pollution\, and biodiv
 ersity loss are intensifying worldwide\, and their heaviest burdens fall 
 on the world's most vulnerable populations and indigenous communities. An
  estimated 1.5 billion people lack basic access to redress for environmen
 tal harms through political\, administrative\, or legal channels. Many of
  these communities also lack skilled advocates\, and the lawyers and nonl
 awyers who do take up their causes face growing harassment and physical a
 ttacks. The <em>Indiana Journal of Global Legal Studies</em> has brought 
 together scholars from across the Americas to examine where marginalized 
 communities\, their advocates\, and the governance systems that too often
  leave them behind intersect.</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p><strong>Panel 1:</str
 ong> Environmental Protection Across Borders: Who Shapes the Rules\, and 
 Who Gets Heard?</p><p><strong>Panel 2:</strong> Effective Environmental R
 epresentation: Bridging the Gap Between Rights and Results</p><p><strong>
 Panel 3:</strong> Environmental Governance Frameworks: What Do Comprehens
 ive Solutions Look Like?</p><p><strong>Panel 4:</strong> In Practice: App
 lying Environmental Rights and Supporting Environmental Defenders</p><p> 
  Papers presented at the symposium will be published in Volume 34 Issue 2
  of the Journal.&#160\;</p>
UID:20261120T144500Z-2464840@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20261027T100702Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2464840-ijgls-symposium
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029T150243Z
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2464840
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
